From bdf1c0f24858e992ec094fe2810a7b6cb3fd412a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JUstin <justinscollo@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:16:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: cpcap: accept Wingray's ST 1.0 revision

The Xoom's CPCAP reports vendor ST and raw revision zero, i.e. 1.0.  The
mainline core rejects every revision below 2.1, so CPCAP probe failed with
-ENODEV before IRQ or input registration.

Accept revision zero and the explicit 1.0 encoding while retaining the
existing floor for other old revisions.  The SPI, interrupt and ON-key
registers used by Image 67 are compatible; regulator/charger drivers remain
disabled.  This is the fix for the power button producing no input device.
---
 drivers/mfd/motorola-cpcap.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/motorola-cpcap.c b/drivers/mfd/motorola-cpcap.c
index 0af117a9..9dfd9748 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/motorola-cpcap.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/motorola-cpcap.c
@@ -82,7 +82,13 @@ static int cpcap_check_revision(struct cpcap_ddata *cpcap)
 		 CPCAP_REVISION_MAJOR(rev), CPCAP_REVISION_MINOR(rev),
 		 rev);
 
-	if (rev < CPCAP_REVISION_2_1) {
+	/*
+	 * Wingray's ST CPCAP 1.0 reports a raw revision of zero.  The
+	 * registers and ON interrupt used by this board are compatible with
+	 * the older part; only the regulator/charger features are omitted.
+	 */
+	if (rev != 0 && rev != CPCAP_REVISION_1_0 &&
+	    rev < CPCAP_REVISION_2_1) {
 		dev_info(&cpcap->spi->dev,
 			 "Please add old CPCAP revision support as needed\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
-- 
